{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>It is the finger of Elohim.</b> This is a plague of the province, for even if it came through the hands of these, we would do the same." "<b>It is the finger of Elohim.</b> Feminine form, with a ḥirik." "<b>And Pharaoh's heart grew strong.</b> Even for this one he did not seek a remedy, because it involved only dust, and his vessels were washed every day; and so is the custom of all the great men — even the poor are constantly accustomed to lice and do not mind them. This plague came without warning, and so was the procedure: for the first two he would warn, and on the third he would strike without warning. For once a person has sinned and repeated, it becomes to him as though permitted — what benefit is there in warning him, since he will not repent? Furthermore, lice, boils' darkness — which were the third plagues, are lethal plagues, and he would not repent upon warning; therefore because they were tripled, Rabbi Yehudah made for them mnemonic signs: דצ״ך עד״ש באח״ב — except for the plague of the firstborn, which is counted with the three latter ones, for it is not proper to fix a whole word for the sake of one letter. And one may say: he made mnemonic signs for them so that people would not say the essence of their occurrence is in the order of Psalms, where it does not count the plagues in the order it counts them here."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "The phrase כנים חושך שחין lists the three third plagues in each group (lice, darkness/boils); translated literally as it appears. The phrase אין נכון לקבוע תיבה בשביל אות אחת is rendered literally; it refers to why 'בכורות' would be needed only for one letter in the mnemonic scheme."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:39.675347762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}